@startuml
title Verify OTP Sequence (/api/auth/otp/verify)

autonumber
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor Guest
boundary "OtpScreen" as OtpScreen
entity "OtpVerifyRequest\n(Request DTO)" as OtpVerifyRequest
control "AuthController" as AuthController
control "AuthService" as AuthService
control "OtpRepository" as OtpRepository
database "VocaNovaDbContext" as DbContext
database "MySQL Database" as MySQL

note over OtpScreen, MySQL
Current code has OTP verification by phone.
No separate verify-email flow was found in Auth code.
end note

Guest -> OtpScreen: Enter OTP code
Guest -> OtpScreen: Click Verify button
OtpScreen -> OtpScreen: Validate OTP input

alt Data input invalid
    OtpScreen --> Guest: Show error message
else Data input valid
    OtpScreen -> OtpVerifyRequest: Create request data\n(phone, otp_code)
    OtpScreen -> AuthController: POST /api/auth/otp/verify\nOtpVerifyRequest
    AuthController -> AuthController: Validate OtpVerifyRequest

    alt Request validation fails
        AuthController --> OtpScreen: HTTP 400 error
        OtpScreen --> Guest: Show error message
    else Request validation success
        AuthController -> AuthService: VerifyOtpAsync(otp data)
        AuthService -> OtpRepository: FindLatestAsync(phone, userId=null)
        OtpRepository -> DbContext: Query latest active OTP
        DbContext -> MySQL: SELECT latest OTP
        MySQL --> DbContext: OTP row or null
        DbContext --> OtpRepository: Result
        OtpRepository --> AuthService: OtpRecord or null

        alt OTP missing or expired
            AuthService --> AuthController: Unauthorized result
            AuthController --> OtpScreen: HTTP 401 error
            OtpScreen --> Guest: Show error message
        else OTP already used
            AuthService --> AuthController: Conflict result
            AuthController --> OtpScreen: HTTP 409 error
            OtpScreen --> Guest: Show error message
        else Too many verify attempts
            AuthService --> AuthController: TooManyRequests result
            AuthController --> OtpScreen: HTTP 429 error
            OtpScreen --> Guest: Show error message
        else OTP code is wrong
            AuthService -> OtpRepository: StageAttemptAsync(otpId, attempt + 1)
            OtpRepository -> DbContext: Update verify attempt count
            DbContext -> MySQL: UPDATE otp_verifications
            MySQL --> DbContext: Update result
            DbContext --> OtpRepository: Save result
            OtpRepository --> AuthService: Attempt saved

            AuthService --> AuthController: Unauthorized result
            AuthController --> OtpScreen: HTTP 401 Invalid OTP
            OtpScreen --> Guest: Show error message
        else OTP valid
            AuthService -> OtpRepository: StageUsedAsync(otp, userId=null)
            OtpRepository -> DbContext: Mark OTP used
            DbContext -> MySQL: UPDATE otp_verifications
            MySQL --> DbContext: Update result
            DbContext --> OtpRepository: Save result
            OtpRepository --> AuthService: OTP verified

            AuthService --> AuthController: Return verify result
            AuthController --> OtpScreen: HTTP 200 OK
            OtpScreen --> Guest: Show success message
        end
    end
end

@enduml
